{"event_type":"review","id":"1807d994a667ef097dcf076a93cf6871bda67ddc9c85e1bdba897d2bdbdbfe41","occurred_at":"2026-11-15T22:48:11Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/ae8606ab382063f98b48c511613bcb39178953d419887f12dde378353ff515b3","sha256":"ae8606ab382063f98b48c511613bcb39178953d419887f12dde378353ff515b3"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/28be5a767221eaeab993d89af0cbfc81a4f99cf309c0917822dfc54840820ec8","sha256":"28be5a767221eaeab993d89af0cbfc81a4f99cf309c0917822dfc54840820ec8"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/1709b6baa8102c386c3d2547cbee1e7bbfb1d166a996f93c54b033e6f349a0cb","sha256":"1709b6baa8102c386c3d2547cbee1e7bbfb1d166a996f93c54b033e6f349a0cb"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/bc591d11ab90151c25660c2f4b61e0095b787fbeda17a0588db423b00d55d323","sha256":"bc591d11ab90151c25660c2f4b61e0095b787fbeda17a0588db423b00d55d323"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/74a5a420d672806638a590a609b5256deeb8e9f38461e8644083bcd734fab1d5","sha256":"74a5a420d672806638a590a609b5256deeb8e9f38461e8644083bcd734fab1d5"}],"attempt_id":"8c87e4cc9509706ec85cdf0a2f44bf324bb718fc35a330c663fe92ce4708d689:0:1","base":"845116bc7e4b296dd1cf1e47b3c9ea1797bb0fa9","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"ceca79f0284170065645b62238b29fcc30202f4d","body":"**Compare `JsonNumber` values before rejecting profile equality.**\n\nIn `src/policy/crq/reviewAdmission.ts:124`, separately decoded `JsonNumber.int(1)` values compare unequal. Thus, identical numeric profiles do not join an existing item.\n\nThe next admission computes the same identity but restarts generation at 1. It creates a duplicate item id. `replaceItem` then replaces both entries with the new item's observer list. Cancelling the new request can cancel work still required by the first request.\n\nAdd value comparison for `JsonNumber` before this fallback. Cover separately decoded numeric profiles and preservation of both observers.","id":"b736b07187d61eddaec75d5156ee8d6729220c000bfdef9b03c5e50a933f711e","intervals":[[124,124]],"path":"src/policy/crq/reviewAdmission.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Compare `JsonNumber` values before rejecting profile equality."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"ceca79f0284170065645b62238b29fcc30202f4d","body":"**Replayed and status responses drop the receipt recovery signal.**\n\nAn adequate item whose receipt cannot be verified returns `receipt-unavailable` and `resubmit` only on the first admission. A replayed admission or a status request returns a completed result with neither field. A client that retries after losing the first reply cannot learn that it must resubmit.\n\n`admit` returns the replayed result before the receipt check. `retryRequest` returns `reviewStatus` unchanged, and `reviewStatus` never emits `receipt-unavailable`. It adds `resubmit` only for an inactive, inadequate item. Make the receipt check run on every response that can report an adequate item. Either pass `verifyReceipt` into the status path, or persist the unavailable-receipt state and emit it from `reviewStatus`. The status and replay callers in `reviewCapability.ts` do not currently have the verified-receipt set in scope, so no local diff is given.","id":"f430a841118d2b0fefb3a66066793edbd4f9959b6e0c520903207199326bce55","intervals":[[349,353]],"path":"src/policy/crq/reviewAdmission.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Replayed and status responses drop the receipt recovery signal."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"ff7ebc64321b66fcdd0029966dd18fd15233030b","body":"**Use an own-property check for the verdict outcome lookup.**\n\n`VERDICT_OUTCOMES` is a plain object literal. A verdict such as `constructor`, `toString`, or `valueOf` resolves through the prototype chain to an inherited function. The `??` fallback does not replace it, because it is not `null` or `undefined`. The function then becomes `outcome` and the event payload. Event hashing rejects it, and the report is quarantined with a serialization error instead of being recorded as `unverified`. Restrict the lookup to own properties.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n   const declared =\n-    submitted.verdict === null ? null : (VERDICT_OUTCOMES[submitted.verdict] ?? 'unverified');\n+    submitted.verdict === null\n+      ? null\n+      : Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(VERDICT_OUTCOMES, submitted.verdict)\n+        ? VERDICT_OUTCOMES[submitted.verdict]\n+        : 'unverified';\n```\n\n</details>","id":"3295a24f28decd2541ff686dbbdc745619460f07f592db655ca50eb940437181","intervals":[[152,152]],"path":"src/policy/crq/reviewRecord.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Use an own-property check for the verdict outcome lookup."}],"head":"4ad1f13b4309d57962f0d51f9f1760ea40a66370","head_tree":"bda143e5c3801b7c35ed31c000807c5f716cf6f6","input_scope":[{"blob":"d89feb1e3c16fd75ec9b121d49ac5046c56fbd0d","intervals":[[1,425]],"path":"src/policy/crq/authorAdmission.ts"},{"blob":"a1a0463def048a93ce8224994adce1464928d40c","intervals":[[1,481]],"path":"src/policy/crq/backfillSubjects.ts"},{"blob":"87bed1ee71c104ad4f344f1235906dad794b5822","intervals":[[1,292]],"path":"src/policy/crq/classification.ts"},{"blob":"615f32e0a383bfc4ea17f732a1efa06c7f0c1044","intervals":[[1,430]],"path":"src/policy/crq/coverageSnapshot.ts"},{"blob":"9d07e9929999e9b3b0abb3e6fe02b98fd2706452","intervals":[[1,373]],"path":"src/policy/crq/notifyDrain.ts"},{"blob":"7300eaba3bb51f1d0afa2dbf475dccbb3dde2ed0","intervals":[[1,336]],"path":"src/policy/crq/recentDiscovery.ts"},{"blob":"ceca79f0284170065645b62238b29fcc30202f4d","intervals":[[1,381]],"path":"src/policy/crq/reviewAdmission.ts"},{"blob":"ff7ebc64321b66fcdd0029966dd18fd15233030b","intervals":[[1,326]],"path":"src/policy/crq/reviewRecord.ts"}],"job_id":"8c87e4cc9509706ec85cdf0a2f44bf324bb718fc35a330c663fe92ce4708d689:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"d89feb1e3c16fd75ec9b121d49ac5046c56fbd0d","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/policy/crq/authorAdmission.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"a1a0463def048a93ce8224994adce1464928d40c","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/policy/crq/backfillSubjects.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"87bed1ee71c104ad4f344f1235906dad794b5822","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/policy/crq/classification.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"615f32e0a383bfc4ea17f732a1efa06c7f0c1044","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/policy/crq/coverageSnapshot.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"9d07e9929999e9b3b0abb3e6fe02b98fd2706452","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/policy/crq/notifyDrain.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"7300eaba3bb51f1d0afa2dbf475dccbb3dde2ed0","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/policy/crq/recentDiscovery.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"ceca79f0284170065645b62238b29fcc30202f4d","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/policy/crq/reviewAdmission.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"ff7ebc64321b66fcdd0029966dd18fd15233030b","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/policy